{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"project":1},{"slug":2,"info_box":3,"info_box_thumb":4,"title":5,"location":6,"description":7,"type":8,"tags":9,"developer":11,"publisher":6,"release_date":12,"date":13,"role":14,"platform":15,"status":16,"links":17,"featured":3,"content":21,"resources":22,"thumbnailMetadata":262},"fitbit-ace-arcade",true,"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/thumbnail.jpg","Fitbit Ace Arcade","Google","11 Games created for the Ace Arcade on the Fitbit Ace LTE, a fitness powered wearable for kids!","Catalogue",[10],"Wearable","Mighty Kingdom","2024 - 2026","2026","Game Lead & Product Manager","Ace Arcade","Released & Unreleased",[18],{"title":19,"url":20},"Google Store","https://store.google.com/us/product/fitbit_ace_lte?hl=en-US","\u003Ch2>What is it?\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>The Fitbit Ace LTE is a device for kids, where being active is rewarded with game-time. We developed a portfolio of 11 games in Unity for the device to date, with additional games developed by Tantalus Media, Mighty Games, and Robot Circus. \u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>Many of our (best) games are still yet to launch, but the ones that have been released include:\u003C/p>\n\u003Ctable style=\"width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-family: sans-serif;\">\n  \u003Cthead>\n    \u003Ctr style=\"background-color: #f2f2f2; border-bottom: 2px solid #ddd;\">\n      \u003Cth style=\"padding: 12px; text-align: left; width:25%;\">Cover\u003C/th>\n      \u003Cth style=\"padding: 12px; text-align: left;\">Preview\u003C/th>\n      \u003Cth style=\"padding: 12px; text-align: left;\">Description\u003C/th>\n    \u003C/tr>\n  \u003C/thead>\n  \u003Ctbody>\n    \u003Ctr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\">\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px;\">\n        \u003Cimg src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/images/ff-cell.png\" style=\"border-radius: 4px;\" />\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle;\">\n        \u003Cvideo width=\"600\" controls> \n          \u003Csource src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/videos/ff_vid.webm\" type=\"video/webm\";>\n        \u003C/video>\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; vertical-align: middle;\">\u003Cb>Frankenforge\u003C/b>\u003Cbr>A monster-building auto-battler. Defeat monsters to take their limbs, build a monster out of them, and fight!\u003C/td>\n    \u003C/tr>\n    \u003Ctr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\">\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px;\">\n        \u003Cimg src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/images/zm-cell.png\" style=\"border-radius: 4px;\" />\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle;\">\n        \u003Cvideo width=\"600\" controls> \n          \u003Csource src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/videos/ww_vid.webm\" type=\"video/webm\";>\n        \u003C/video>\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; vertical-align: middle;\">\u003Cb>Zoomies\u003C/b>\u003Cbr>Control a cat on a robot vacuum, in this physics-destruction game, to destroy the house to prevent an alien invasion.\u003C/td>\n    \u003C/tr>\n    \u003Ctr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\">\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px;\">\n        \u003Cimg src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/images/gh-cell.png\" style=\"border-radius: 4px;\" />\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle;\">\n        \u003Cvideo width=\"600\" controls> \n          \u003Csource src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/videos/gh_vid.webm\" type=\"video/webm\";>\n        \u003C/video>\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; vertical-align: middle;\">\u003Cb>Gnome Heisters\u003C/b>\u003Cbr>Form a crew and pull-off heists in this DnD-like story generator. Play microgames to train them before their big heist! \u003C/td>\n    \u003C/tr>\n    \u003Ctr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\">\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px;\">\n        \u003Cimg src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/images/sp-cell.png\" style=\"border-radius: 4px;\" />\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle;\">\n        \u003Cvideo width=\"600\" controls> \n          \u003Csource src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/videos/sp_vid.webm\" type=\"video/webm\";>\n        \u003C/video>\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; vertical-align: middle;\">\u003Cb>Sproutlings\u003C/b>\u003Cbr>Take care of your virtual pet! Find insects and fruits to watch it evolve as you feed it new combinations! \u003C/td>\n    \u003C/tr>\n        \u003Ctr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\">\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px;\">\n        \u003Cimg src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/images/sg-cell.png\" style=\"border-radius: 4px;\" />\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle;\">\n        \u003Cvideo width=\"600\" controls> \n          \u003Csource src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/videos/sg_vid.webm\" type=\"video/webm\";>\n        \u003C/video>\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; vertical-align: middle;\">\u003Cb>Spirit Garden\u003C/b>\u003Cbr>Build your forests, summon spririts, and regenerate the islands in this mindful idle game.\u003C/td>\n    \u003C/tr>\n    \u003C/tr>\n        \u003Ctr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\">\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px;\">\n        \u003Cimg src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/images/jj-cell.png\" style=\"border-radius: 4px;\" />\n      \u003C/td>\n      \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; font-weight: bold; vertical-align: middle;\">\n        \u003Cvideo width=\"600\" controls> \n          \u003Csource src=\"/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/videos/jj_vid.webm\" type=\"video/webm\";>\n        \u003C/video>\n      \u003C/td>\n            \u003Ctd style=\"padding: 12px; vertical-align: middle;\">\u003Cb>Jelly Jam\u003C/b>\u003Cbr>Listen and follow the dance moves as the watch tracks and scores your movements. Asmass enough fans to move on to bigger venues!\u003C/td>\n    \u003C/tr>\n  \u003C/tbody>\n\u003C/table>\n\n\u003Ch2>So what did I actually do?\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>I was primarily responsible for leading the team, and the creative design of the games, as well as engaging with the client and making sure they&#39;re loving what we&#39;re giving them around the gameplay, and IP alignment. \u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>As we needed to be developing two games in parallel, keeping the scope tight throughout the project was a key requirement, while still adapting to what we found gave players the most value in play. This also included setting our specific milestone requirements, roadmapping, and epic, task, and story-point management, to make sure we&#39;re hitting our targets. \u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>In additional to my general design and production responsabilities, a brief list of additional duties across the life of these projects includes:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Prototype development\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Localization implementation\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>UI implementation\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Developing key features, and technical art systems (C#)\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>On-device debugging via Android Studio, and bug fixing\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Liasing with translators, and providing transliteration notes\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Release management, and deliverables via Gerrit\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>QA / LQA\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Writing game cheats for partner QA team\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Essentially at points I&#39;ve done a bit of everything you could do while making a game... except actual art, definitely not art...\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Notable Info\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Since I can&#39;t go into everything, here are some of the more unqiue, but general elements of these projects:\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch3>Playtime\u003C/h3>\n\u003Cp>The playtime requirements of these games needed to follow, what I like to call, a 5-4-90 rule. That being that kids should play:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>5\u003C/strong> minute game sessions,\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>4\u003C/strong> times per day,\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>for \u003Cstrong>90\u003C/strong> days\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Cp>So essentially each of these games \u003Cem>needed\u003C/em> to have \u003Cstrong>30 hours\u003C/strong> of content, which was TOUGH to design and plan for sometimes, expecially with the 6 month turnaround. \u003C/p>\n\u003Ch3>Gameplay and Sensors\u003C/h3>\n\u003Cp>A tenent of the gameplay for all games was to integrate the device sensors in meaningful ways. That being the gyro, altimeter, accelerometer, magnometer, light, and touch.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>This ranged from being simple, but, core game features, as in the case of \u003Cstrong>Zoomies\u003C/strong>, where you tilt the watch to control the character movement. \u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>Then extended to more micro-game-esque in \u003Cstrong>Gnome Heisters\u003C/strong>, where you trained the Gnomes for your Heist by completing a series of goofy, several-second-long challenges, such as blowing on the screen to extinguish the burning Gnome. \u003C/p>\n\u003Ch3>Custom Tooling\u003C/h3>\n\u003Cp>Because the watch was propriatary, and had a custom SDK to interface with, getting the team to be always playing builds on-device was a challenge, expecially for the less technically inclined members who did not enjoy using a terminal to install builds, or pull logs. \u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>To minimize the friction, I developed an in-house GUI tool to allow the team to one-click install builds to their device from a remote build-agent, start the games, take screenshots, pull logs, etc. \u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>This majorly improved the on-device testing throughout the team, and we got much better buy-in from the team on the project overall, better feedback, and faster turnaround of device-related features.\u003C/p>\n",{"images":23,"videos":242,"documents":261},[24,85,136,155,170,185,200],{"name":25,"path":26,"hasWebP":3,"metadata":27},"ff-cell.png","/microfolio/content/projects/fitbit-ace-arcade/images/ff-cell.png",{"credit":28,"source":28,"description":28,"headline":28,"keywords":28,"camera":28,"lens":28,"focalLength":28,"aperture":28,"shutterSpeed":28,"iso":28,"dateTime":28,"gps":28,"city":28,"state":28,"country":28,"location":28,"raw":29,"creditLine":28},null,{"xmp":30,"png":57,"pngFile":79,"pngText":80,"file":81},{"_raw":31,"about":32,"OriginalDocumentID":35,"DocumentID":38,"InstanceID":41,"CreatorTool":44,"DerivedFrom":47},"\u003C?xpacket begin=\"ï»¿\" id=\"W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d\"?> \u003Cx:xmpmeta xmlns:x=\"adobe:ns:meta/\" x:xmptk=\"Adobe XMP Core 9.1-c003 79.9690a87fc, 2025/03/06-20:50:16        \"> \u003Crdf:RDF xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\"> \u003Crdf:Description rdf:about=\"\" xmlns:xmpMM=\"http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/mm/\" xmlns:stRef=\"http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/sType/ResourceRef#\" xmlns:xmp=\"http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/\" xmpMM:OriginalDocumentID=\"xmp.did:3c7934db-4191-477a-850e-f1b4b9cd620e\" xmpMM:DocumentID=\"xmp.did:8484C97F4E6E11F093B1D10C5E30A7E1\" xmpMM:InstanceID=\"xmp.iid:8484C97E4E6E11F093B1D10C5E30A7E1\" xmp:CreatorTool=\"Adobe Photoshop 24.7 (Macintosh)\"> \u003CxmpMM:DerivedFrom stRef:instanceID=\"xmp.iid:66b46606-361f-4466-a478-7991be696d23\" stRef:documentID=\"adobe:docid:photoshop:3fdc4493-9540-be41-b7eb-e5cf8cf4f134\"/> \u003C/rdf:Description> \u003C/rdf:RDF> \u003C/x:xmpmeta> \u003C?xpacket end=\"r\"?>",{"value":33,"attributes":34,"description":33},"",{},{"value":36,"attributes":37,"description":36},"xmp.did:3c7934db-4191-477a-850e-f1b4b9cd620e",{},{"value":39,"attributes":40,"description":39},"xmp.did:8484C97F4E6E11F093B1D10C5E30A7E1",{},{"value":42,"attribut